# Projections: the forms of projecting activation rows by weights, written
# once per backend and taken by an entry's native declaration with one
# `project` line (`seismic/lang/src/projection.rs`). The formals: M
# activation rows, K columns, N rows of each weight, WEIGHTS the weights one
# activation row serves (`paired`: two, a gate and an up weight whose
# products one epilogue combines; `single`: one), W a weight in `each`,
# `any`, `agree` or an `each W:` block.

# Second-level weight scales (every entry reading packed weights): one
# `<weight>_scale` port per weight, after every other argument, in weight
# order, `[S] f32` per tensor (or `[S, E] f32` per expert in the routed
# entries). S = 1 carries the scale (NVFP4 `.scale`), applied to that
# projection's F32 accumulator before anything else (`scale_rows`); S = 0 is
# no scale, and the natives compile the scaling out. S is static on every
# backend.

# Packing bounds (the entries with a token-packing form: `dense_expand`,
# `dense_output`, `project_rows`, `attention_output`, `attention_project`,
# `gated_delta_project`): one `<weight>_bound` port per packed weight, after
# the scales, `[B] f32`. B = K / n carries the weight's packing bound
# (`packing_bound`, `WeightPlan::bound`): per run of the n columns that share
# a scale, the largest squared l2 norm of a row's codes minus their centre,
# over the tensor's rows, which certifies a packed operand's gain for this
# tensor rather than for every row of the format. B = 0 is no bound. No
# result depends on it but a packed form's, whose error it lowers; B is
# static on every backend. On Metal a bound offers the packed form's wider
# residue (`RESIDUE` 2: one more bit of top sum, half the top token's step),
# which applies only to weights whose packed entries are 8 bits
# (`forms::metal_packing`): the declarations admit it only for a bounded
# weight whose codes take it (`form(W, PACK_RESIDUE)`).

# Metal: the K1 projection library (`metal/lib/projection/`, the form bodies
# in `operator.h`). Output rows below BATCH_FROM run the GEMV launch
# (SIMDGROUPS x ROWS lane groups of LANES lanes per threadgroup, each owning
# weight rows; LANES sets the reduction order, so it is arithmetic; TILED = 1
# is the form one or two output rows may take over `rows32` weights: the
# same weight rows per threadgroup, a thread owning one of them and a
# simdgroup's lanes consecutive rows of a tile, with a summation order of its
# own, `gemv_tile_row`; TILED = 2 is the row mapping walked by packet class
# over `rows32` weights, `gemv_classes`, with the row mapping's results under
# the same LANES; the launch for three rows up does not offer it, the walk's
# threadgroup rounds cost more than it gains there). An entry launches it
# three times, `gemv` for one row, `gemv_pair` for two and `gemv_rows` for
# three rows up to BATCH_FROM, each with its own mapping and each
# instantiating only the row bounds it runs: the fastest mapping of one row
# is not that of several (on the M4 Pro 8 simdgroups of 8 lanes a group, a
# group owning two weight rows, or one where the projection is paired), and a
# row's result is the same in both only under the same LANES (and TILED).
# The entry's prologue forms the GEMV's rows in-threadgroup, so a decode
# projection is one launch; in larger classes the entry's own pre-pass first
# writes its rows to scratch.
# BATCH_FROM..16 rows the batched launch on the matrix units (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS
# x BATCH_ROWS blocks of 8 weight rows, F32 operands, a different summation
# order, so BATCH_FROM is arithmetic too; with MATRIX = 1, which the
# projection admits only over weights with a matrix form (`form(W, MATRIX)`,
# which `forms::metal_matrix` admits: integer lane codes under factors per
# 256 columns, or direct scales per 32), the launch takes the matrix GEMV
# instead, `gemv_matrix`: the weights' integer codes as the left fragment,
# BATCH_PARTS simdgroups sharing a fragment's eight weight rows, a summation
# order of its own); 17..64 rows the GEMM at the fixed small-row geometry
# (`gemm_small`: 32 x 64 tiles, 4-way split-K where the projection is
# single); larger classes the GEMM over tuned TILE_M x TILE_N tiles
# (activations staged as stored, weights decoded to half once per tile), with
# SPLIT-way split-K where the projection is single (a paired epilogue reads
# whole sums).
# TALL selects the tall GEMM past 64 rows (`gemm_tall`): TALL_M rows by 32
# weight rows per threadgroup, STAGERS staging simdgroups decoding the
# weights once for all its rows, TALL_K columns per stage, and the
# activations read from device memory. On simdgroup matrices they are read in
# fragment order: a paired entry's pre-pass writes that order, and a single
# projection first reorders its rows into `fragments` (a second copy of them,
# in whole 64-row tiles). The form needs K a multiple of 128 and has no
# split-K; its staged producer reads every weight, dense ones included
# (`forms` admits it for all), and where it is admitted it is the default,
# with the same results as the tiles above.
# PACK selects the token-packing GEMM past 64 rows (`gemm_packed`, over the
# weights `forms::metal_packing` admits, integer lane codes not scaled by a
# power of two of their own whose coefficients fold per run of a 32-column
# block, on a device without tensor operations, and where paired a gate and
# an up weight one operand serves, whose runs and entry widths agree:
# `form(W, PACK)` of each weight, and the same `PACK_FOLDS` and
# `PACK_RESIDUE`); devices with tensor operations run the staged tile, with
# its results, in the `unpacked` launch, and each launch of the other path
# returns at once): the activations become integer codes per (row, 32
# columns) and two rows share one F32 matrix operand against the weights'
# stored codes, so a row's result depends on the row it is packed with
# (`int8_token_packing`). A simdgroup multiplies PACK_TOKENS operand
# fragments (16 rows each) by 8 / PACK_TOKENS weight fragments (8 weight rows
# each), four of them a threadgroup (independent tiles; a gate and an up
# simdgroup pair where paired); WEIGHTS_AHEAD loads a block's weight words
# one block ahead (the best of both differs by device and shape). The
# `where` holds the form's launch parameters at their defaults outside the
# form, and the staged and tall tiles' inside it, where they are not
# launched, so the form's configurations do not multiply another's. Its
# scratch is transient, per call: the packed operand (`packed`, 2 bytes per
# padded row and column, plus one step read ahead), the rows' scales and
# code sums, or for 8-bit entries (`PACK_RESIDUE`) the rows' scales and the
# RESIDUE low bit planes of their codes (`token_factors`, 4 bytes per padded
# row and 32 columns, 8 with two planes; RESIDUE 2 takes a packing bound,
# `bound(W)`, and applies only to weights whose packed entries are 8 bits)
# and each weight's block scales and biases (`<stem>_factors`, 4 bytes per
# weight row and 32 columns), both held over one power of two per row
# (`token_scales`, `<stem>_scales`, 4 bytes a row; a weight tile's 32 rows
# share theirs) so that the F16 fold cannot overflow. Packed and quantized
# operands pad the rows to TOKENS, 64 where paired (a tile serves both
# weights) and 128 where single.
# INT8 selects the int8 GEMM past 64 rows over the weights `form(W, INT8)`
# admits: the rows quantized per (row, 32 columns), each weight's block
# coefficients and biases, then the int8 tiles.
projection dense for metal:
    let TOKENS = 128 / WEIGHTS
    let SPLITS = 1 for paired
    let SPLITS = SPLIT for single
    let SMALL_SPLITS = 1 for paired
    let SMALL_SPLITS = 4 for single
    params (arithmetic BATCH_FROM in [5, 3, 9, 2] default 5, arithmetic SPLIT in [1, 2, 4] default 1 for single, form TALL in [1, 0] default 1,
        arithmetic form INT8 in [0, 1] default 0, arithmetic form PACK in [0, 1] default 0, arithmetic form RESIDUE in [1, 2] default 1)
    where (TALL == 0 or (SPLITS == 1 and K % 128 == 0))
    where (INT8 == 0 or (TALL == 1 and K % 512 == 0 and N % (64 / WEIGHTS) == 0 and each(W, form(W, INT8) == 1) and agree(W, form(W, INT8_INTERLEAVED))))
    where (INT8 == 1 or INT8_TILE == 128) for single
    where (PACK == 0 or (TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and K % 256 == 0 and K < 1048576 and N % (64 / WEIGHTS) == 0 and each(W, form(W, PACK) == 1) and agree(W, form(W, PACK_FOLDS)) and agree(W, form(W, PACK_RESIDUE))))
    where (PACK == 1 or (PACK_TOKENS == 4 and WEIGHTS_AHEAD == 0))
    where (PACK == 0 or (TILE_M == 64 and TILE_N == 64))
    where (PACK == 0 or (TALL_M == 128 and TALL_K == 64 and STAGERS == 2))
    where (RESIDUE == 1 or (PACK == 1 and any(W, bound(W) > 0 and form(W, PACK_RESIDUE) == 1)))
    where (MATRIX == 0 or (K % 256 == 0 and each(W, form(W, MATRIX) == 1))) for paired
    where (MATRIX == 0 or each(W, form(W, MATRIX) == 1)) for single
    scratch partials bytes (SPLIT * M * N * 4) when M > 64 and SPLIT > 1 for single
    scratch small_partials bytes (4 * M * N * 4) when M > 16 and M <= 64 for single
    scratch fragments bytes (ceil_div(M, 64) * 64 * K * 2) when M > 64 and TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and PACK == 0 for single
    scratch packed bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * K * 2 + 1024) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch token_factors bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * (K / 32) * 4 * RESIDUE) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    each W:
        scratch factors bytes (N * (K / 32) * 4) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch token_scales bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * 4) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    each W:
        scratch scales bytes (N * 4) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch quantized bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * K) when M > 64 and INT8 == 1
    scratch row_scales bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * (K / 32) * 2) when M > 64 and INT8 == 1
    scratch block_sums bytes (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS * ceil_div(K, 1024) * 32 * 2) when M > 64 and INT8 == 1
    each W:
        scratch coefficients bytes (N * (K / 32) * 4) when M > 64 and INT8 == 1
        scratch biases bytes (ceil_div(N, 32) * 32 * ceil_div(K, 1024) * 32 * 2) when M > 64 and INT8 == 1
    launch gemv when M < 2:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [16, 8, 4, 2, 32] default 16, ROWS in [1, 2] default 1, arithmetic LANES in [16, 32, 8] default 16,
            arithmetic form TILED in [0, 1, 2] default 0)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(min(ceil_div(K, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448) * 64, TILED * SIMDGROUPS * (128 * WEIGHTS)))
    launch batch when M >= BATCH_FROM and M <= 16:
        params (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS in [8, 4, 16, 32] default 8, BATCH_ROWS in [2, 1, 4] default 2,
            arithmetic BATCH_PARTS in [2, 4, 1] default 2, arithmetic form MATRIX in [1, 0] default 1)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 8) * BATCH_PARTS, BATCH_SIMDGROUPS), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(16640, min((BATCH_SIMDGROUPS * 256 + ceil_div(K, 32) * 32) * ceil_div(M, 8), 28672)))
    launch gemm_small when M > 16 and M <= 64:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 64 / WEIGHTS), ceil_div(M, 32), SMALL_SPLITS)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch reduce_small for single when M > 16 and M <= 64:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch gemm when M > 64 and TALL == 0:
        params (TILE_M in [64, 128, 32] default 64, TILE_N in [64, 128] default 64)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, TILE_N / WEIGHTS), ceil_div(M, TILE_M), SPLITS)
        threads_per_threadgroup (max(TILE_M, 64) * TILE_N / 32, 1, 1)
    launch reduce for single when M > 64 and SPLIT > 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch relayout for single when M > 64 and TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and PACK == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(M, 64) * K, 256), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch tall when M > 64 and TALL == 1 and INT8 == 0 and PACK == 0:
        params (TALL_M in [128, 256, 512] default 128, TALL_K in [64, 128] default 64, STAGERS in [2, 1] default 2)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 32 / WEIGHTS), ceil_div(M, TALL_M), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup ((TALL_M / 32 + STAGERS) * 32, 1, 1)
    launch quantize when M > 64 and INT8 == 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * TOKENS, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch coefficients when M > 64 and INT8 == 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N * (K / 256), 1024), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch int8 for paired when M > 64 and INT8 == 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 32), ceil_div(M, 64), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch int8 for single when M > 64 and INT8 == 1:
        params (INT8_TILE in [128, 64] default 128)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, INT8_TILE), (INT8_TILE / 128) * ceil_div(N, 32) + (1 - INT8_TILE / 128) * ceil_div(N, 64), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch gemv_rows when M >= 3 and M < BATCH_FROM:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [8, 16, 4, 2, 32] default 8, ROWS in [1, 2] default 1 for paired, ROWS in [2, 1] default 2 for single,
            arithmetic LANES in [8, 16, 32] default 8, arithmetic form TILED in [0, 1] default 0)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(min(ceil_div(K, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448) * 64, TILED * SIMDGROUPS * (128 * WEIGHTS)))
    launch gemv_pair when M == 2 and M < BATCH_FROM:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [8, 16, 4, 2, 32] default 8, ROWS in [1, 2] default 1 for paired, ROWS in [2, 1] default 2 for single,
            arithmetic LANES in [8, 16, 32] default 8, arithmetic form TILED in [0, 1, 2] default 0)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(min(ceil_div(K, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448) * 64, TILED * SIMDGROUPS * (128 * WEIGHTS)))
    launch pack when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        reads (RESIDUE)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * (TOKENS / 4), 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch pack_coefficients when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        threadgroups (N / 32, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch packed when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        params (PACK_TOKENS in [4, 2] default 4, WEIGHTS_AHEAD in [0, 1] default 0)
        reads (RESIDUE)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, TOKENS) * N / 32, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch unpacked when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 64 / WEIGHTS), ceil_div(M, 64), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)

# CUDA: the K1 projection library (`cuda/common/projection.cuh`). Every K1
# CUDA entry runs the GEMV to 16 rows and the GEMM beyond, in two row bands.
# The GEMV is the 16-bit path (the A-rounded activation in bf16/f16 MMAs
# against exact codes, rows independent of the row count): `gemv` to 8 rows,
# `gemv16` (two 8-row column blocks) from 9 to 16; 8 warps per block in groups
# of KSPLIT that split K and reduce in part order. The small-band GEMM
# (`gemm_small`, 17 to 64 rows: 64-row block tiles, 3 cp.async stages) has
# two operand paths: the 16-bit path (weights dequantized to A) and the INT8
# candidate (arithmetic INT8 = 1: activations quantized per 32 codes as q8_1
# does, s8 MMAs), which `where` admits only for weights the int8 GEMM takes
# (`form(W, INT8)`); the tuner keeps INT8 only where it is faster within
# tolerance. The large-band GEMM (`gemm`, beyond 64 rows: 128-row block
# tiles, 2 stages) is the 16-bit path; each stage's copies are issued by one
# of ROTATE rotating warp sets (the launch parameter ROTATE, tuned: its best
# value depends on the weight representation, and the arithmetic does not,
# so every value gives the same bits; likewise in the `gemm` launches of
# `attention`, `recurrent`, `readout` and `draft`). Entries with few output
# columns split either band over K up to 128 rows (grid z: 2 shares of
# partials that `finalize` sums in part order). Measured on GB10 (17 to 512
# rows, both paths, split 1/2/4, tiles 32/64/128): up to 64 rows want the
# 64-row tiles, beyond them the 128-row ones, the few-column entries the
# split up to 128 rows. Staging launches form the rows a launch does not
# read in place: `stage` a normalized input's A rows (at one row the GEMV
# block forms its row in its shared memory instead), the shared operand
# stage the INT8 candidate's q8_1 rows plus (d, d * sum q) groups.

# CPU: the CPU projection library (`cpu/lib/projection/projection.rs`).
# INT8 is a form on every CPU projection, as on Metal: INT8 = 1 quantizes
# the staged rows to Q8 blocks and runs the representation's integer dot
# (VNNI or AVX2 products, NEON SDOT, eight-row tiles over four activation
# rows), a different algorithm from the F32 dot whose best ROWS and
# participant counts say nothing about the F32 form's. `where` admits it
# where a weight it multiplies takes the quantized dot (`form(W, INT8)`:
# floating dense weights and packed weights but those whose products take
# NVFP4 operand rows, which multiply the rows their recipe forms). As a form its one
# representative is measured right after the defaults, before any F32
# refinement. As a plain parameter it came after the three ROWS moves:
# gemma-4-e2b QAT Q4 on an EPYC 9V45 (8 cores, 60 s) measured only its
# default for dense_expand (43% of the objective), and project_rows reached
# INT8 sixth, at 16 us against the F32 form's 278 us per decode row.

# A plain projection of A rows, published in Y: F32 where a row op consumes
# the projection before the residual (`post_norm_residual`'s projected rows:
# attention and feed-forward outputs of post-norm blocks, the per-layer
# input's projection back to the hidden width), A where it feeds another
# projection (Nemotron's latent down).
#
# A block-diagonal weight of G groups: each row's columns split into G
# consecutive runs of K, and run g projects through its own block of N
# weight rows, `weight[g * N : (g + 1) * N]`, into output columns
# g * N .. (g + 1) * N (DeepSeek V4.1's grouped attention output). The
# ungrouped projection is G = 1. One scale and bound cover the whole tensor.
fn project_rows[M, G, K, N, WS, WB](source: &tensor[M, G * K] A, weight: &tensor[G * N, K] W,
    weight_scale: &tensor[WS] f32, weight_bound: &tensor[WB] f32) -> tensor[M, G * N] Y
    where G >= 1 and WS >= 0 and WS <= 1 and WB >= 0 and (WB == 0 or K % WB == 0):
    # The rows are dense activations: staging them in A (an exact copy)
    # states that domain, which the CUDA forms' A staging requires.
    let mut rows = tensor[M, G * K] A
    parallel for row in 0..M:
        rows[row] = source[row]
    let mut sum = tensor[M, G * N] f32
    let mut result = tensor[M, G * N] Y
    for group in 0..G:
        linear(rows[:, group * K : (group + 1) * K], weight[group * N : (group + 1) * N],
            sum[:, group * N : (group + 1) * N])
    scale_rows(sum, weight_scale, result)
    return result

# Metal: the `attention_output` launch structure (GEMV below BATCH_FROM rows,
# batched GEMV to 16, the fixed small GEMM with its 4-way split to 64, tuned
# GEMM beyond with SPLIT-way split-K summed in order by `finalize`) with a
# store epilogue in Y. TALL selects the tall GEMM past 64 rows and PACK the
# token-packing form, both as in `attention_output` (`relayout` reorders the
# source rows into `fragments`; the PACK form's launches, error class and
# transient scratch are `dense_output`'s, the weights' factors per 32-row
# weight tile).
#
# Groups: every launch but the G = 1 forms' runs group g at grid z (z = g in
# the GEMV, batched, finalize, relayout and tall launches, z = g * split +
# part in the GEMMs), over the group's source columns, weight rows and
# output columns, and its own G-th of the split partials and of the tall
# form's fragments. The packed, matrix and NVFP4-operand forms stage or pack
# the whole source row or weight, and run only G = 1.
native project_rows for metal from "metal/project_rows.metal":
    static (G, K, N, WS, WB)
    params (arithmetic BATCH_FROM in [5, 3, 9, 2] default 5, arithmetic SPLIT in [1, 2, 4] default 1, form TALL in [1, 0] default 1,
        arithmetic form PACK in [0, 1] default 0, arithmetic form RESIDUE in [1, 2] default 1)
    where WS <= 1 and (G == 1 or (PACK == 0 and MATRIX == 0 and operands(W) == 0)) and (TALL == 0 or (SPLIT == 1 and K % 128 == 0)) and (PACK == 0 or (TALL == 1 and K % 256 == 0 and K < 1048576 and N % 64 == 0 and form(W, PACK) == 1)) and (PACK == 1 or (PACK_TOKENS == 4 and WEIGHTS_AHEAD == 0)) and (PACK == 0 or (TILE_M == 64 and TILE_N == 64)) and (PACK == 0 or (TALL_M == 128 and TALL_K == 64 and STAGERS == 2)) and (RESIDUE == 1 or (PACK == 1 and WB > 0 and form(W, PACK_RESIDUE) == 1)) and (MATRIX == 0 or form(W, MATRIX_SYMMETRIC) == 1)
    scratch partials bytes (SPLIT * G * M * N * 4) when M > 64 and SPLIT > 1
    scratch small_partials bytes (4 * G * M * N * 4) when M > 16 and M <= 64
    scratch fragments bytes (G * ceil_div(M, 64) * 64 * K * 2) when M > 64 and TALL == 1 and PACK == 0
    scratch packed bytes (ceil_div(M, 128) * 128 * K * 2 + 1024) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch token_factors bytes (ceil_div(M, 128) * 128 * (K / 32) * 4 * RESIDUE) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch weight_factors bytes (N * (K / 32) * 4) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch token_scales bytes (ceil_div(M, 128) * 128 * 4) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch weight_scales bytes (N * 4) when M > 64 and PACK == 1
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when M >= BATCH_FROM and operands(W) == 1
    launch project_rows_gemv when M < BATCH_FROM:
        params (SIMDGROUPS in [16, 8, 4, 2, 32] default 16, ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1, arithmetic LANES in [16, 32] default 16)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (min(ceil_div(K, 32) * (min(M, 2) + 2 * min(M / 3, 1) + 4 * min(M / 5, 1)), 448) * 64)
    launch project_rows_stage when M >= BATCH_FROM and operands(W) == 1:
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_batch when M >= BATCH_FROM and M <= 16:
        params (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS in [8, 4, 16, 32] default 8, BATCH_ROWS in [2, 1, 4] default 2,
            arithmetic BATCH_PARTS in [2, 4, 1] default 2, arithmetic form MATRIX in [1, 0] default 1)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 8) * BATCH_PARTS, BATCH_SIMDGROUPS), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (BATCH_SIMDGROUPS * 32, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (max(16640, min((BATCH_SIMDGROUPS * 256 + ceil_div(K, 32) * 32) * ceil_div(M, 8), 28672)))
    launch project_rows_gemm_small when M > 16 and M <= 64:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 64), ceil_div(M, 32), 4 * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_finalize_small when M > 16 and M <= 64:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_gemm when M > 64 and TALL == 0:
        params (TILE_M in [64, 128, 32] default 64, TILE_N in [64, 128] default 64)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, TILE_N), ceil_div(M, TILE_M), SPLIT * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (max(TILE_M, 64) * TILE_N / 32, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_finalize when M > 64 and SPLIT > 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_relayout when M > 64 and TALL == 1 and PACK == 0:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(M, 64) * K, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_tall when M > 64 and TALL == 1 and PACK == 0:
        params (TALL_M in [128, 256, 512] default 128, TALL_K in [64, 128] default 64, STAGERS in [2, 1] default 2)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 32), ceil_div(M, TALL_M), G)
        threads_per_threadgroup ((TALL_M / 32 + STAGERS) * 32, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_pack when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        reads (RESIDUE)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, 128) * 32, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_pack_coefficients when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        threadgroups (N / 32, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_packed when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        params (PACK_TOKENS in [4, 2] default 4, WEIGHTS_AHEAD in [0, 1] default 0)
        reads (RESIDUE)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M, 128) * N / 32, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_unpacked when M > 64 and PACK == 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, 64), ceil_div(M, 64), 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (128, 1, 1)

# Vulkan: the `attention_output` form (GEMV to 8 rows, GEMM beyond with
# SPLIT-way split-K summed in order by `finalize`, over NVFP4 weights the
# source rows' operands the stage launch forms into `staged`). Groups as on
# Metal: every launch but the stage runs group g at grid z (z = g in the GEMV
# and finalize launches, z = g * SPLIT + part in the GEMM) over the group's
# source columns, weight rows and output columns, and its own G-th of the
# split partials; the NVFP4-operand form stages the whole source row and runs
# only G = 1.
native project_rows for vulkan from "vulkan/project_rows.comp":
    static (G, K, N, WS)
    params (SIMDGROUPS in [16, 8, 4, 2, 32] default 16, ROWS in [1, 2, 4] default 1, arithmetic LANES in [16, 32] default 16,
            TILE_M in [128, 64, 32] default 64, TILE_N in [128, 64] default 128, SUB_M in [32, 64] default 32, SUB_N in [32, 64] default 32,
            arithmetic SPLIT in [1, 2, 4] default 1)
    let GEMV_GROUPS = ceil_div(N, SIMDGROUPS * ROWS * 32 / LANES)
    let GEMV_THREADS = SIMDGROUPS * 32
    let GEMV_SHARED = 256 + 32 * operands(W) + min(8 * ceil_div(K, 32), 288) * 72
    where (G == 1 or operands(W) == 0) and SUB_M <= TILE_M and SUB_N <= TILE_N and WS <= 1
    scratch partials bytes (SPLIT * G * M * N * 4) when M > 8 and SPLIT > 1
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * 2) when M > 8 and operands(W) == 1
    launch project_rows_stage when M > 8 and operands(W) == 1:
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (128)
    launch project_rows_gemv1 when M <= 1:
        threadgroups (GEMV_GROUPS, 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (GEMV_THREADS, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_SHARED)
    launch project_rows_gemv2 when M == 2:
        threadgroups (GEMV_GROUPS, 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (GEMV_THREADS, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_SHARED)
    launch project_rows_gemv4 when M >= 3 and M <= 4:
        threadgroups (GEMV_GROUPS, 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (GEMV_THREADS, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_SHARED)
    launch project_rows_gemv8 when M >= 5 and M <= 8:
        threadgroups (GEMV_GROUPS, 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (GEMV_THREADS, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (GEMV_SHARED)
    launch project_rows_gemm when M > 8:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, TILE_N), ceil_div(M, TILE_M), SPLIT * G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (TILE_M * TILE_N * 32 / (SUB_M * SUB_N), 1, 1)
        shared_bytes ((TILE_M + TILE_N) * 80)
    launch project_rows_finalize when M > 8 and SPLIT > 1:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)

# `attention_output`'s bands (GEMV to 16 rows reading the rows in place, the
# INT8 candidate on either matrix band, split-K to 128 rows) with a store
# epilogue in Y.
#
# Groups: every launch but the stage runs group g at grid z (z = g in the
# GEMV and finalize launches, z = g * split + part in the GEMMs), over the
# group's source columns, weight rows and output columns, and its own G-th
# of the split partials. A group's weight rows start on a whole 16-row tile
# (N % 16 == 0). The staged forms (INT8, OPERAND, NVFP4 operands) stage the
# whole source row and run only G = 1.
native project_rows for cuda from "cuda/project_rows.cu":
    static (G, K, N, WS)
    params (arithmetic INT8 in [0, 1] default 0, arithmetic OPERAND in [0, 1] default 0)
    where K % 64 == 0 and WS <= 1 and (G == 1 or (N % 16 == 0 and INT8 == 0 and OPERAND == 0 and operands(W) == 0)) and (OPERAND == 0 or INT8 == 0) and (INT8 == 0 or form(W, INT8) == 1)
    scratch staged bytes (M * K * max(1 + OPERAND, 2 * operands(W))) when (M > 1 and operands(W) == 1) or (M > 16 and (INT8 == 1 or OPERAND == 1))
    scratch groups bytes (M * K / 4) when INT8 == 1 and M > 16
    scratch partials bytes (2 * G * M * N * 4) when M > 16 and M <= 128
    launch project_rows_stage when (M > 1 and operands(W) == 1) or (M > 16 and (INT8 == 1 or OPERAND == 1)):
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        threadgroups (M, 1, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_gemv when M <= 8:
        params (arithmetic KSPLIT in [4, 2, 8] default 4)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8 / KSPLIT), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (operands(W) * (1 - min(1, M - 1)) * K * 2)
    launch project_rows_gemv16 when M > 8 and M <= 16:
        params (arithmetic KSPLIT in [4, 2, 8] default 4)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8 / KSPLIT), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_gemm_small when M > 16 and M <= 64:
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8), 1, G * (1 + min(1, 128 / M)))
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (3 * (64 * 144 + 10240) + 2048)
    launch project_rows_gemm when M > 64:
        params (ROTATE in [2, 1, 4] default 2)
        reads (INT8, OPERAND)
        threadgroups (ceil_div(ceil_div(N, 16), 8), ceil_div(M, 128), G * (1 + min(1, 128 / M)))
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)
        shared_bytes (2 * (128 * 144 + 10240) + 2048)
    launch project_rows_finalize when M > 16 and M <= 128:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(M * N, 256), 1, G)
        threads_per_threadgroup (256, 1, 1)

# Groups: the stage launch stages each row's G runs of K as G staged rows
# (work item (row, group)), and the row launch's work item (item, group)
# projects the group's ROWS weight rows against its staged rows.
native project_rows for cpu from "cpu/project_rows.rs":
    static (WS)
    params (ROWS in [8, 4, 2, 1] default 8, arithmetic form INT8 in [0, 1] default 0)
    where WS <= 1 and (INT8 == 0 or form(W, INT8) == 1)
    scratch quantized bytes (G * ceil_div(M, Q8_ROWS) * Q8_ROWS * ceil_div(K, Q8_VALUES) * Q8_BYTES)
    scratch staged bytes (G * M * K * 4)
    launch project_rows_stage:
        threadgroups (M, G, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (1, 1, 1)
    launch project_rows_rows:
        threadgroups (ceil_div(N, ROWS), G, 1)
        threads_per_threadgroup (1, 1, 1)
